AG CuteMusic on macOS
=====================

Development: the app from this checkout
---------------------------------------

As AG CuteSync (macos/ there): a venv, py2app's alias mode, the app in ~/Applications.

  brew install python gstreamer pygobject3
  bash macos/install.sh

install.sh makes a venv (~/work/ag-cutemusic-env) from Homebrew's python with --system-site-packages, so it sees
Homebrew's gi (GStreamer), installs PyQt6, mutagen and py2app (macos/requirements.txt) into it, builds the app
(macos/make-app.sh) into ~/Applications and adds an `ag-cute-music` command. Re-run it after moving this checkout.

The alias bundle runs the cutemusic package of this checkout, so edits apply on the next launch; it does not run on
another Mac (GStreamer and its plugins come from Homebrew, which py2app does not carry), and it does not update
itself (updater.py: the standalone app only).

To run without any app: bin/ag-cute-music, with a python that has PyQt6 and gi.


The standalone app: to copy to other Macs
-----------------------------------------

Everything in the bundle: Python 3.10+ from python.org (its universal2 installer, not Homebrew's), PyQt6, and
GStreamer from its own Python wheels (pip install gstreamer-bundle), no Homebrew.

  macos/make-standalone.sh              (default, --universal) arm64 + x86_64: runs natively on both; Qt's two
                                        wheels merged with delocate-merge
  macos/make-standalone.sh --intel      x86_64 only, built under Rosetta (rarely needed: Intel Macs run the
                                        universal app)

It builds in its own venv (build/standalone-<mode>-env, log build/py2app-<mode>.log), trims GStreamer and Qt to what
the app uses (prune_app.py), builds the AG Podcast Mixer driver into it (below), checks every binary has the
architectures needed, then:

- signs it: Developer ID, hardened runtime (sign-app.sh: each binary, the frameworks, the driver, the app; signatures
  cached in build/sign-cache); ad hoc when there is no Developer ID Application certificate, or SIGN_IDENTITY=-
- self test (AG_CUTEMUSIC_SELFTEST=1, standalone.py): GStreamer and the elements playing needs, every cutemusic
  module imported, no library loaded from outside the app. An app failing it is not packaged: the script stops
  (exit 1), with no image nor zip, and removes those of an earlier build
- signed with Developer ID: the disk image dist/AG-CuteMusic.dmg (make-dmg.sh, needs create-dmg from MacPorts),
  notarized (notarize-app.sh, keychain profile NOTARY_PROFILE, default notarytool-password; - to skip), its ticket
  stapled to the image and the app, dist/AG-CuteMusic.zip, and the image opened (NO_OPEN=1: not)

The app is dist/<mode>/AG CuteMusic.app (mode universal or intel; the Intel image and zip are named -intel). Ad hoc
signed or not notarized, on the other Mac: xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine "/Applications/AG CuteMusic.app".

standalone.py, the bundle's start script, uses only the Python packages inside the bundle (a PyQt6 installed with
pip --user would otherwise be loaded next to the bundle's own Qt).


Releasing and updates
---------------------

  macos/release.sh [<version>]

1. raises __version__ in cutemusic/__init__.py (default: its last number + 1; pushed, it also starts the Windows
   build on GitHub)
2. adds a debian/changelog entry, "Bug fixes", and opens it in $VISUAL / $EDITOR (else TextEdit) to be edited: its
   bullets are the release notes the update dialog shows; asks before building
3. make-standalone.sh (universal)
4. make-appcast.py: dist/AGCuteMusicAppcast.xml (Sparkle's format: the version, its notes, each image with its
   length and sha256), shown; asks before upload.sh

Run again after a failed build or an upload not done: while __version__ is not the live appcast's version yet, it is
kept with its changelog entry (no second bump).

  macos/upload.sh

Uploads a release over ssh (rsync) to download:/var/www/download/Cute/ (UPLOAD_TO=<host:folder>), served as
https://download.ag-projects.com/Cute/: the image(s), notarized, their zips, then the appcast, last, after checking
the built app is __version__.

The standalone app, Developer ID signed, reads https://download.ag-projects.com/Cute/AGCuteMusicAppcast.xml at start
and once a day ("Check for updates automatically", in the update dialog) and from AG CuteMusic -> Check for
Updates...; a newer version is offered with its notes (Install Update, Skip This Version, Remind Me Later).
Installed: the image downloaded and checked against its sha256, its app checked (same bundle id, the version
announced, codesign --verify --deep --strict, the same Developer ID team, notarized), copied beside the app; the app
quits, the new one is swapped in (the administrator's password only when its folder is not writable) and started.
An Intel image has its own entry, taken by the Intel app (AGCuteMusicBuild in its Info.plist), only when built and
uploaded.


The AG Podcast Mixer driver
---------------------------

macos/driver/ (python3-sipsimple docs/PodcastMixerLink.md, v2): a CoreAudio driver (AudioServerPlugIn, libASPL
vendored in macos/driver/libASPL) whose "AG Podcast Mixer" input is the mixer's mix, Blink's microphone (Blink Pro's
too); the mixer plays into its hidden "AG Podcast Mixer Feed" output. Needs cmake (brew install cmake).

  macos/driver/build.sh [--trace] [--sign]   build/driver/AGPodcastMixer.driver, arm64 + x86_64, macOS 13+
  sudo macos/driver/install.sh [-u]          into /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL (or removed), coreaudiod restarted

make-standalone.sh builds it into the app (Contents/Resources). The app installs, updates or removes it from
Play -> ... AG Podcast Mixer driver... (the administrator's password; the sound stops a moment while coreaudiod
restarts) and offers the install or update at start, once per driver version (DRIVER_VERSION in
macos/driver/CMakeLists.txt: raise it with every change to the driver).


Files
-----

  install.sh, make-app.sh, ag-cute-music.py  the development app (alias mode) and its start script
  setup.py, requirements.txt                 py2app's recipe (both apps), the venv's packages
  make-standalone.sh, standalone.py          the standalone app, its start script and self test
  prune_app.py                               GStreamer plugins and Qt modules trimmed to what the app uses
  sign-app.sh, entitlements.plist            Developer ID signing, hardened runtime
  notarize-app.sh                            notarization and stapling
  make-dmg.sh, dmg-background.png            the drag-to-Applications disk image
  release.sh, make-appcast.py, upload.sh     a release: version, changelog, build, appcast, upload
  driver/                                    the AG Podcast Mixer driver
  make_icns.py                               the .icns: the VU meters (cutemusic/appicon.py; or an SVG)
